---
import MinistryPage from '../layouts/MinistryPage.astro';
import hero from '../assets/img/uploads/preschool_main_photo.jpg';
import s1 from '../assets/img/uploads/preschool_section_one_1_photo.jpg';

const gallery = Object.values(
  import.meta.glob('../assets/img/uploads/preschool_gallery_*.jpg', { eager: true, import: 'default' })
) as ImageMetadata[];
---
<MinistryPage
  title="Preschool Ministry"
  heroSubtitle={"A secure, nurturing environment for infants through Kindergarteners where biblical truths are taught as a foundation for salvation and Christian living.\nThe Preschool Department opens 15 minutes before the start of worship, Sunday School, and AWANA classes."}
  heroImage={hero}
  sectionTitle="Growing Like Jesus Grew"
  sectionImage={s1}
  gallery={gallery}
>
  <p class="italic text-navy font-semibold">
    "And Jesus increased in wisdom and stature, and in favor with God and men." — Luke 2:52
  </p>
  <p>
    Our goals for the growth of infants, toddlers, and preschoolers are based on the fact that they
    grow just as Jesus grew — mentally (in wisdom), physically (in stature), socially and emotionally
    (in favor with man), and spiritually (in favor with God). Therefore we seek to:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
    <li>Lay a strong spiritual foundation in the life of each child we teach, with the hope that when older, each child will accept Christ as their Savior.</li>
    <li>Help children begin to understand God is our creator and giver of all good things, and Jesus is God's Son and our best friend.</li>
    <li>Teach that the Bible is a true and special book that tells about God and Jesus.</li>
    <li>Make church a happy, clean, and safe place to learn Bible truths.</li>
    <li>Provide activity-based teaching with Bible-learning activities that build problem solving, sharing, kindness, and learning to love others.</li>
    <li>Partner with the home in nurturing the spiritual growth of the young child.</li>
    <li>Encourage parents and guardians to actively participate in worship, Bible study, fellowship, and ministry opportunities.</li>
  </ul>
</MinistryPage>
